From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 15:50:58 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] soc: qcom: pmic_glink_altmode: Mask the V2 notification
 fields

When the PAN_EN request selects version 1 ("V2") pin-assignment
notifications, the firmware packs a protocol version into bits 5-7 of
the orientation byte and a reset request into bits 5-7 of the mux byte.
The Surface Laptop 8's ACPI tables describe the same layout (the BORI,
BVER, BMUX and BRST fields of PBUF in its DSDT).

The driver uses both bytes whole, so a V2 notification decodes as an
unknown orientation and an unknown mux state, and the port is forced to
the safe state.

Use only the orientation bits (1:0) and the mux state bits (3:0), and
log the version and reset fields at debug level. All valid orientation
and mux values fit in these bits, so notifications in the legacy format
are handled as before.

This prepares for requesting V2 notifications on Glymur.

Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/soc/qcom/pmic_glink_altmode.c | 21 ++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/qcom/pmic_glink_altmode.c b/drivers/soc/qcom/pmic_glink_altmode.c
index 91a839985d1..c4b378144dc 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/pmic_glink_altmode.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/pmic_glink_altmode.c
@@ -491,7 +491,7 @@ static void pmic_glink_altmode_sc8280xp_notify(struct pmic_glink_altmode *altmod
 	const struct usbc_sc8280x_tbt_data *tbt;
 	const struct usbc_sc8280x_dp_data *dp;
 	const struct usbc_notify *notify;
-	u8 orientation;
+	u8 orientation, version, mux_ctrl, reset;
 	u8 port;
 
 	if (len != sizeof(*notify)) {
@@ -503,7 +503,22 @@ static void pmic_glink_altmode_sc8280xp_notify(struct pmic_glink_altmode *altmod
 	notify = data;
 
 	port = notify->port_idx;
-	orientation = notify->orientation;
+	/*
+	 * V2 pin-assignment notifications (PAN_EN argument with version 1) pack
+	 * a protocol version into bits 5-7 of the orientation byte and a reset
+	 * request into bits 5-7 of the mux byte; the DSDT's PBUF layout (BORI,
+	 * BVER, BMUX, BRST) documents the fields. Mask them off so a V2 message
+	 * does not read as an unknown orientation.
+	 */
+	orientation = notify->orientation & 0x3;
+	version = notify->orientation >> 5;
+	mux_ctrl = notify->mux_ctrl & 0xf;
+	reset = notify->mux_ctrl >> 5;
+
+	dev_dbg(altmode->dev,
+		"PAN port %u orientation %u version %u mux %u reset %u vid %#x svid %#x ext %*ph\n",
+		port, orientation, version, mux_ctrl, reset, le16_to_cpu(notify->vid),
+		svid, (int)sizeof(notify->extended_data), &notify->extended_data);
 
 	if (port >= ARRAY_SIZE(altmode->ports) || !altmode->ports[port].altmode) {
 		dev_dbg(altmode->dev, "notification on undefined port %d\n", port);
@@ -513,7 +528,7 @@ static void pmic_glink_altmode_sc8280xp_notify(struct pmic_glink_altmode *altmod
 	alt_port = &altmode->ports[port];
 	alt_port->orientation = pmic_glink_altmode_orientation(orientation);
 	alt_port->svid = svid;
-	alt_port->mux_ctrl = notify->mux_ctrl;
+	alt_port->mux_ctrl = mux_ctrl;
 
 	if (svid == USB_TYPEC_DP_SID) {
 		dp = &notify->extended_data.dp;
-- 
